From: "keepup[bot]" <keepup[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: route messages with TypeSafe Jev behind a setting

The model router starts a headless agent whose only job is to call
select_category with one label from a fixed list. TypeSafe's Jev is built for
that job: a Choice question returns one option from a supplied list and a
probability for each option.

With ROUTER_CLASSIFIER=jev and a TYPESAFE_API_KEY, classifyWithJev() asks Jev
first. classifyWithLLM() is unchanged and stays the fallback when the chosen
option's probability is under 0.70, the call fails, or there is no key.

The log says which path answered: a fall back logs why before the agent runs,
and what the agent returned after it has, so a failed agent never reads as an
answer.

A "none" at or above 0.70 is final and means no rule matched, so the agent
isn't paid to repeat it. A "none" under 0.70 goes to the agent, because a
weak "none" can hide a rule that should have matched.

The default stays "agent", so nothing changes until a person switches it on.
This calls POST /v1/systemone with fetch, so it adds no dependency, and it
pins jev-1.14.0 because an alias can move under a fixed threshold.

